24
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:02,438
uncommonly conscientious for a seaman and endued with a deep natural reverence

25
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:07,318
the wild watery loneliness of his life did therefore strongly incline him to

26
00:02:07,319 --> 00:02:11,478
superstition but to that sort of superstition which in some organizations

27
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:16,679
seems rather to spring somehow from intelligence than from ignorance outward

28
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:21,559
portance and inward presentiments were his and if at times these things bent

29
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:26,758
