41
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:29,559
Starbucks was no crusader after perils.

42
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:34,598
In him courage was not a sentiment but a thing simply useful to him and always at

43
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:40,118
hand upon all mortally practical occasions. Besides, he thought perhaps

44
00:03:40,119 --> 00:03:44,039
that in this business of whailing, courage was one of the great staple

45
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:48,519
outfits of the ship, like her beef and her bread, and not to be foolishly

46
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:54,199
wasted. Therefore, he had no fancy for lowering for whales after sundown, nor

47
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:59,636
for persisting in fighting a fish that too much persisted in fighting him. Four

48
00:03:59,637 --> 00:04:03,877
thought Starbucks, I am here in this critical ocean to kill whales for my

49
00:04:03,878 --> 00:04:09,158
living and not to be killed by them for theirs. And that hundreds of men had

50
00:04:09,159 --> 00:04:12,118
been so killed. Starbucks well knew.

51
00:04:12,119 --> 00:04:16,758
What doom was his own fathers? Where in the bottomless deeps could he find the

52
00:04:16,759 --> 00:04:22,598
torn limbs of his brother. with memories like these in him, and moreover given to

53
00:04:22,599 --> 00:04:27,239
a certain superstitiousness, as has been said, the courage of this Starbucks,

54
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:32,438
which could nevertheless still flourish, must indeed have been extreme. But it

55
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:36,999
was not in reasonable nature that a man so organized, and with such terrible

56
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:42,039
experiences and remembrances as he had, it was not in nature that these things

57
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:46,918
should fail in latently engendering an element in him which, under suitable

58
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:51,877
circumstances, would break out from its confinement, and burn all his courage

59
00:04:51,878 --> 00:04:57,877
up. and brave as he might be. It was that sort of bravery chiefly visible in

60
00:04:57,878 --> 00:05:03,399
some intrepid men, which while generally abiding firm in the conflict with seas

61
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:07,956
or winds or whales or any of the ordinary irrational horrors of the

62
00:05:07,957 --> 00:05:13,559
world, yet cannot withstand those more terrific because more spiritual terrors

63
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:20,519
which sometimes menace you from the concentrating brow of an enraged and mighty man.

64
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:24,679
But were the coming narrative to reveal in any instance the complete abasement

65
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:29,399
of poor Starbucks fortitude, scarce might I have the heart to write it, for

66
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:34,199
it is a thing most sorrowful, nay shocking, to expose the fall of valor in

67
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:40,278
the soul. Men may seem detestable as joint stock companies and nations,

68
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:46,438
naves, fools, and murderers there may be. Men may have mean and meager faces,

69
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:52,598
but man in the ideal is so noble and so sparkling, such a grand and glowing

70
00:05:52,599 --> 00:05:57,318
creature that over any ignaminious blemish in him all his fellows should

71
00:05:57,319 --> 00:06:02,679
run to throw their costliest robes. That immaculate manliness we feel within

72
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:07,158
ourselves, so far within us that it remains intact, though all the outer

73
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:11,717
characters seem gone, bleeds with keenest anguish at the undraped

74
00:06:11,718 --> 00:06:18,118
spectacle of a valor ruined man. Nor can piety itself at such a shameful sight

75
00:06:18,119 --> 00:06:23,318
completely stifle her upbridings against the permitting stars. But this august

76
00:06:23,319 --> 00:06:28,359
dignity I treat of is not the dignity of kings and robes, but that abounding

77
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:31,399
dignity which has no robed investature.

78
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:36,039
Thou shalt see it shining in the arm that wields a pick or drives a spike.

79
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:41,079
That democratic dignity which on all hands radiates without end from God

80
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:45,956
himself, the great God absolute, the center and circumference of all

81
00:06:45,957 --> 00:06:51,318
democracy, his omnipresence, our divine equality.

82
00:06:51,319 --> 00:06:55,956
If then to meanest mariners and renegades and castaways, I shall

83
00:06:55,957 --> 00:07:02,598
hereafter ascribe high qualities, though dark, weave round them tragic graces, if

84
00:07:02,599 --> 00:07:06,918
even the most mournful, per chance the most abased among them all, shall at

85
00:07:06,919 --> 00:07:11,717
times lift himself to the exalted mounts. If I shall touch that workman's

86
00:07:11,718 --> 00:07:17,717
arm with some ethereal light, if I shall spread a rainbow over his disastrous set

87
00:07:17,718 --> 00:07:23,239
of sun, then against all mortal critics, bear me out in it, thou just spirit of

88
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:28,839
equality, which has spread one royal mantle of humanity over all my kind.

89
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:33,956
Bear me out in it, thou great democratic god, who dit not refuse the swart

90
00:07:33,957 --> 00:07:37,079
convict Bunan, the pale poetic pearl.

91
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:41,636
Thou who dit clothed with doubly hammered leaves of finest gold the

92
00:07:41,637 --> 00:07:46,758
stumped and poppered arm of old cervantes. Thou who dit pick up Andrew

93
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:51,956
Jackson from the pebbles. Who dst hurl him upon a warhorse. Who d thunder him

94
00:07:51,957 --> 00:07:57,478
higher than a throne. Thou who in all thy mighty earthly marchings ever

95
00:07:57,479 --> 00:08:06,400
culllest thy selectest champions from the kingly commons. Bear me out in it, oh God.
